SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction to Garlic Cultivation Using Drip Irrigation Technology</h2>\n<p>Garlic is a bulbous plant widely used in the food and pharmaceutical industries. Planting garlic requires attention to planting timing, proper bulb density, and precise water resource management. In traditional methods, flood irrigation often leads to water waste and root diseases in garlic. However, using <strong>drip irrigation</strong> and <strong>tip lines</strong>, temperature and moisture can be kept constant within the root zone. This method not only results in water savings of up to 30-40%, but also promotes uniform bulb growth and increased yield per hectare by enhancing moisture consistency. Indeed, precise root zone moisture management is fundamental to achieving final bulb quality in hot and semi-arid climates, where a significant portion of the country\'s garlic farms are located.</p>\n\n<h2>Soil Preparation and Garlic Planting</h2>\n<p>Before installing the irrigation system, substrate preparation is crucial. Soil should have an optimal pH (approximately 6 to 7) and proper drainage. Garlic responds well to sandy loam soils. The preparation and planting steps include the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Plowing and harrowing:</strong> To eliminate weeds and aerate the soil.</li>\n<li><strong>Harvesting and transport:</strong> Use high-quality seed (bulbs) that are free from fungal diseases.</li>\n<li><strong>Planting distances:</strong> Row spacing is usually set at 25 to 30 cm and in-row plant spacing at 15 to 20 cm to allow passage of irrigation tips.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To accurately implement spacing, you can follow the general measurement principles per hectare explained in the article <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D9%85%D9%84%D9%88%D9%86-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Melon Yield Per Hectare</a> as a model; because understanding precision in material and plantable space is the key to cost management. Additionally, detailed analysis of planting density based on local conditions can make a significant difference in final yield. In this regard, considering environmental and seed genetic factors is of high importance. For more details on how to calculate density and its effect on crop quality, it is essential to study articles related to precise measurements per hectare. <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D9%85%D8%A7%D8%B1%DA%86%D9%88%D8%A8%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Fava Bean Yield Per Hectare</a> It can also serve as a suitable model for understanding the production cycle of vegetables and root/tuber crops, although there are subtle differences in nutritional and irrigation requirements. Ultimately, familiarity with mushroom yield per hectare as an example of high value-added products helps you, as a farm manager, develop a more analytical approach to crop planning.</p>\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-کاشت-سیر-با-آبیاری-قطرهای-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع کاشت سیر با آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>planting methods drip crop irrigation schedule garlic</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Installation of tape and drip systems for garlic</h2>\n<p>Tape drip is one of the most efficient methods for growing garlic, as it delivers moisture directly near the roots. Selecting the appropriate tape depends on row spacing. Tapes with a drip emitter spacing of 10 to 15 centimeters are ideal for garlic. Proper installation of the tapes must be done after the seeds or cloves are fully established to avoid root damage. Precision at this stage directly affects the uniformity of water distribution and prevents clogging of the emitters.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create precise and clean furrows.</li>\n<li>Plant the cloves at a depth of 5 to 10 centimeters.</li>\n<li>Cover the cloves with soil.</li>\n<li>Install the tape drip in the center of the row or on the bed shoulder, depending on the planting method.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For step-by-step installation instructions, refer to the guide on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/drip-irrigation-tape-installation-steps-ariq/">Drip Tape Irrigation Installation Steps</a> which is useful. Important points such as appropriate operating pressure (1 to 3 bars) and the use of filters to prevent emitter clogging are explained in detail in that resource. Additionally, familiarity with <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/tarzi-nasbi-lulayi-ob-yori-tip/">Tape Irrigation Pipe Installation Method</a> can be beneficial, as the general principles of pipe installation are shared between these two methods, with the main difference being the type of emitter and its placement. Furthermore, understanding how to manage pressure and flow in distribution networks requires knowledge of hydraulic principles, which are fully explained in the key points for selecting water tape drip.</p>\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-کاشت-سیر-با-آبیاری-قطرهای-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع کاشت سیر با آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>planting methods drip crop irrigation schedule garlic</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Timing and irrigation schedule for garlic</h2>\n<p>Irrigation scheduling is the most critical part of drip system use. Garlic is sensitive to moderate moisture during the vegetative growth phase (before bulb formation). In the late season, during bulb formation, irrigation requirements decrease to prevent bulb rot. In the final stage (stem drying) before harvest, irrigation is stopped. These gradual changes in water dosage require precise monitoring of plant growth.</p>\n<table border="1" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">\n<tr><th>Garlic growth stage</th><th>Irrigation requirement</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Germination to Vegetative Growth</td><td>Medium</td><td>Maintain uniform soil moisture for leaf development</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bulb formation</td><td>Gradual reduction</td><td>Prevent rot and improve internal quality</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Stem senescence</td><td>Cessation of irrigation</td><td>A few weeks before harvest for bulb maturation</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The best method is monitoring soil moisture. If using smart systems, utilize data from smart stations to adjust irrigation doses precisely according to crop needs. Understanding how to calculate dose and interval based on crop requirements is critical in this context. Monitoring moisture in the root zone is key to successful onion quality control.</p>\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-کاشت-سیر-با-آبیاری-قطرهای-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع کاشت سیر با آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>planting methods drip crop irrigation schedule garlic</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Practical tips and secondary care</h2>\n<p>In addition to irrigation, fertigation via drip is one of the major advantages of this system. You can deliver liquid fertilizers directly to the roots with water. This enhances uptake of specific nutrients for garlic, such as potassium (during bulb formation). Furthermore, weed control is slightly more difficult in drip systems due to lower surface moisture, but it remains manageable with appropriate herbicides and drainage management. Using mulch can help reduce the need for herbicides.</p>\n<p>One important tip is preventing fungal diseases by ensuring adequate ventilation. Although drip irrigation manages root moisture, heavy soils still pose a risk of poor drainage. It is recommended to improve soil structure with compost before the season begins. Also, monitoring irrigation water pH and hardness is essential to prevent clogging in drippers. Ionic balance in the nutrient solution is a primary factor in maintaining plant health.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>Is drip irrigation water for garlic different from sprinkler irrigation?</h3>\n<p>Yes, drip irrigation maintains root temperature and promotes more uniform growth, whereas sprinklers may spray disease spores onto leaves, which is detrimental to garlic.</p>\n<h3>Is the drip tape recyclable?</h3>\n<p>Some drip tape models feature a UV-resistant layer and are suitable for 1 to 2 seasons, but annual replacement is recommended to maintain flow quality.</p>\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>Using drip irrigation and drip tape in garlic cultivation brings a revolutionary change to farm management. From increased crop yield to reduced labor costs, these systems are a sustainable and economical option. By following planting principles, selecting the appropriate drip tape, and implementing an irrigation schedule, you can achieve export-quality produce. For further reading on factors that increase yield in grain and vegetable crops, you can refer to articles related to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/rye-harvest-per-hectare-factors-increase-yield/">increasing radish yield per hectare</a> and comparing them with green crops. Your farm success is the result of combining scientific knowledge with operational precision.</p>','Comprehensive Guide to Garlic Cultivation Using Drip and Micro-Sprinkler Irrigation','Garlic is a high-value crop that can achieve excellent yields with proper irrigation management. This guide examines the principles of garlic cultivation using modern drip and tape irrigation technologies to ensure both water conservation and increased farm productivity. From soil preparation to the irrigation calendar and drainage management, everything is covered in this comprehensive article.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
