START TRANSACTION;
SET @source_post_id=(SELECT post_id FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE meta_key='_navar_queue_item_id' AND meta_value='article-content-queue:crop-120' LIMIT 1);
SET @translation_id=(SELECT post_id FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key' AND meta_value='article-translation:crop-120:en-US' LIMIT 1);
SET @slug_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name='cotton-cultivation-drip-tti-irrigation-guide' AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
SET @resolved_slug=IF(@slug_conflict IS NULL,'cotton-cultivation-drip-tti-irrigation-guide','cotton-cultivation-drip-tti-irrigation-guide-crop-120-en');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
SET @resolved_slug=IF(@resolved_conflict IS NULL,@resolved_slug,'cotton-cultivation-drip-tti-irrigation-guide-crop-120-en-df8b1f60');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Why does cotton require drip irrigation?</h2>\n<p>Cotton cultivation, especially in arid and semi-arid regions, faces significant challenges in water resource management. Traditional surface irrigation methods, such as flood irrigation, have consistently been associated with issues like high evaporation, weed growth, and fungal diseases caused by wet foliage. Drip irrigation systems, and specifically the use of Drip Tape, have revolutionized cotton farming. By delivering water directly to the Root Zone, this system maintains optimal moisture levels and minimizes plant water stress. In addition to water conservation, this method enables direct plant nutrition through Fertigation, resulting in more uniform growth and reduced fruit drop. To get the best start, understanding the yield quantities of sugar beet and maize and comparing them can help better understand the system\'s efficiency potential under similar conditions, although cotton has specific sensitivities. You can start by reviewing <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/mohdath-intaj-thur-maksikhi-li-l-hektar-daleel-shamil-lil-muzariin/">Maximum extractable nutrient amount per hectare</a> a look at the yield potential of similar products.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Prerequisites for establishing Drip Tape for cotton cultivation</h2>\n<p>Before planting cotton seeds, proper preparation of the irrigation network is critical. Drip tape is a suitable tool because it has lower installation costs than fixed drip lines and offers a single-use lifespan (typically 1 to 3 years). One of the most important considerations is selecting the appropriate emitter spacing. For cotton, an emitter spacing of 30 to 50 cm on the drip line is generally ideal, as it ensures uniform water distribution around the plant. Additionally, you must consider pre-purchase guidelines for irrigation drip tape to prevent emitter clogging and ensure adequate pressure. Proper installation of the tapes should coincide with seed planting so that roots are in contact with moisture-retaining seeds from the start of the process. Main and lateral lines must be configured to deliver uniform pressure throughout the length of the tapes. To better understand the technical structure, referring to agricultural drip tape connections can help in correctly attaching fittings and preventing hidden leaks.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-کاشت-پنبه-با-آبیاری-قطرهای-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع کاشت پنبه با آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>planting methods drip crop irrigation schedule cotton</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Irrigation and fertilization schedule for cotton</h2>\n<p>Cotton irrigation management must be adjusted based on plant growth stages. Cotton requires regular and moderate irrigation, and severe drought causes flower and fruit drop. In the initial vegetative stage, short and frequent irrigations are more beneficial. As the plant reaches flowering and square initiation, water demand peaks. Combining irrigation with fertilization (Fertigation) via drip tape is a powerful tool. You can use nutrient solutions containing nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium. For more accurate calculation of nutritional needs, knowing <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/mikorit-khomi-yufa-hamadoni-dar-hektar/">Raw micronitrate content per hectare</a> or similar compounds can help regulate precision foliar sprays, although this information is more relevant to animal products, general plant nutrition principles remain applicable. The table below provides a general guide for recommended water application per hectare based on growth stages:</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-کاشت-پنبه-با-آبیاری-قطرهای-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع کاشت پنبه با آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>planting methods drip crop irrigation schedule cotton</figcaption></figure>\n\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Growth Stage</th>\n<th>Irrigation Intensity (cm/week)</th>\n<th>Number of Irrigation Events</th>\n<th>Key Nutrition Points</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Cuttings (Day 1 to 21)</td>\n<td>5-8</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Reduce nitrogen, focus on phosphorus for root development</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rapid growth (Day 21 to 50)</td>\n<td>10-15</td>\n<td>2-3</td>\n<td>Gradual increase in nitrogen</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flowering and flower formation (Day 50 to 70)</td>\n<td>12-18</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Potassium and calcium input, precise boration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fruit growth (Day 70 to 95)</td>\n<td>15-20</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>High potassium to increase seed weight</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pre-harvest (Day 95 onward)</td>\n<td>0-5 (gradual cessation)</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Cut off water and nutrition to induce mild stress</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n\n\n<h2>Practical tips on planting and weed management</h2>\n<p>Cotton planting with the drip-tape method provides an excellent opportunity for weed control, as the shade cast by the drip line limits weed growth. However, management remains necessary. One effective method is the use of plastic mulch or biodegradable covers, though this is more costly. If mulch is not used, surface weeds must be controlled before the planting rows close and the soil is fully covered by cotton leaves. Mechanical methods, such as loosening the soil with appropriate tools or using high-precision pre-planting herbicides, are recommended. Remember that the greater the spacing between cotton planting rows, the more space is created for weed growth; therefore, dense rows with double-sided drip-tape coverage is the optimal state for weed control. Additionally, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/tarzi-nasbi-lulayi-ob-yori-tip/">Ordering of drip-tape rows</a> should be arranged so that the overlap of rows in furrows and sub-lines is minimized to maintain mechanical access.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-کاشت-پنبه-با-آبیاری-قطرهای-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع کاشت پنبه با آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>planting methods drip crop irrigation schedule cotton</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Answers to Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Is a tape drip line more suitable for cotton than a flushable drip line?</strong><br>For cotton, which is typically a one-year annual crop, tape drip lines are more cost-effective. Flushable drip lines (usually with 16 mm lateral diameters) are generally selected for longer-lived perennial crops such as fruit trees. Cotton requires a lower initial investment, and tape drip lines meet this need. Additionally, flushable drip lines sometimes have smaller orifices that are prone to clogging when water has high sediment content, whereas modern tape drip lines feature robust internal intake filters.</li>\n<li><strong>How much water can each drip emitter deliver to the cotton?</strong><br>The water volume per emitter is adjusted based on the spacing between emitters. Typically, a 40 cm spacing on 16 mm laterals delivers approximately 2 to 3 ml/hour per emitter. To achieve adequate root zone depth, irrigation duration must be adjusted so that the wetted zone depth is approximately 30 to 40 cm.</li>\n<li><strong>Can tape drip lines be used in consecutive cotton crops?</strong><br>Yes, but replacement is usually recommended every 1 to 2 seasons. Cotton roots grow directly along the tape line, and after harvest, the tape is either left in the ground or collected. The service life of standard tape drip lines in soils with high salinity and sediment is less than one season.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Conclusion and final recommendations</h2>\n<p>Using drip irrigation and tape drip lines in cotton cultivation is a sustainable and efficiency-oriented solution. By adhering to precise planting principles, scheduled irrigation calendars, and smart nutrient management, it can be expected that cotton fiber quality will improve and losses due to water stress will be reduced to zero. For farmers who are also considering other crops, understanding basic principles such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/barley-yield-per-hectare-factors-increase/">Factors increasing drip line yield per hectare</a> also helps provide a more comprehensive understanding of irrigation management for other crops. The more precise the irrigation system is, the greater the flexibility in variable climatic conditions will be. Additionally, attention to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%81%D8%A7%D8%B5%D9%84%D9%87-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%AA%DB%8C%D9%BE-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%84%D9%88%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7/">Type drip tape for beans</a> which shares similar root structure and water requirements with cotton, can provide better understanding of the physiological principles of stress-sensitive plants. Ultimately, regular monitoring of soil moisture using manual probes or automatic sensors is the key to successful operation of this technology.</p>\n\n','Comprehensive Guide to Cotton Cultivation Using Drip and TTI (Tape Taper Inlet) Irrigation Systems','Cotton is one of the most important agricultural commodities, requiring precise water and nutrient management. This comprehensive guide introduces you to cotton planting principles combined with drip and tape strip irrigation. From network setup to irrigation and fertilization schedules, we will cover all practical aspects to help you achieve a high-quality, high-yield crop. Using tape strip irrigation not only reduces water consumption but also promotes better rooting and reduces weed growth.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
