SET @resolved_slug=IF(@resolved_conflict IS NULL,@resolved_slug,'garlic-seed-quantity-per-hectare-crop-165-en-2869e641');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>Farmers are always seeking ways to optimize costs and increase yields. One of the common questions is <strong>the amount of garlic seed per hectare</strong> . Accurately determining this amount is not just a dry number but a key to resource management, reducing energy consumption in sowing, and ultimately increasing crop profitability. In this guide, we explain the calculation process from start to finish so that you can proceed with purchasing and sowing seed with confidence.</p><h2>Why is accurate calculation of garlic seed quantity per hectare important?</h2><p>Garlic seed, due to specific characteristics such as the need for deep planting and slow root establishment, requires precise planning. If you have used similar calculation guides for crops, you will have noticed that the final plant density is directly linked to the volume of seed used. For garlic, this density must allow for the full growth of cloves without excessive competition between roots causing yield reduction.</p><h3>Factors affecting seed density determination</h3><ul><li><strong>Variety type:</strong> Large-clove varieties require more space.</li><li><strong>Seed Quality:</strong> Germination percentages vary between fresh seeds and those from different suppliers.</li><li><strong>Planting Method:</strong> Modern planting machinery offers higher precision than manual planting.</li><li><strong>Regional Climate:</strong> In drier regions, irrigation management plays a key role in spacing selection; consult specialized sugar beet irrigation research to review similar concepts.</li></ul><><h2>Formulas for Calculating Garlic Seed Quantity per Hectare</h2><p>For accurate calculation, two main variables are required: row spacing (meters) and spike spacing (centimeters). Assume a row spacing of 15 centimeters and a spike spacing of 5 centimeters. This results in approximately 20 planting spike positions per meter of row length.</p><ol><li>Calculating the number of rows per hectare: One hectare equals 10,000 square meters. If the row spacing is 15 centimeters (0.15 meters), the number of rows is 10,000 divided by 0.15, which results in approximately 66,666 rows (assuming field width). However, a simpler method is to consider the area of one linear meter of row. The total row width is divided by the field width.</li><li>Calculating cloves per linear meter: The bulb spacing is 5 centimeters, so 20 cloves fit in one meter.</li><li>Calculating total cloves: Number of longitudinal rows × 20 cloves per meter × field length. A simpler formula for a theoretical estimate is: (1,000,000 / row width) × (100 / bulb width). If the row width is 0.15 m and the bulb width is 0.05 m: (1,000,000 / 0.15) × (1 / 0.05) does not calculate correctly; instead, calculate the number of rows across the field width (assuming 100 meters in length for each row in a 10,000 square meter block). The best method: Calculate the area of each bulb. The area allocated to each bulb = 15 centimeters × 5 centimeters = 75 square centimeters. For one hectare (10,000,000 square centimeters), the number of bulbs is 10,000,000 divided by 75, which equals 133,333 bulbs. Therefore, you need 133,333 cloves.</li></ol><p>To convert the number of cloves to seed weight, you need the clove size. A medium garlic clove weighs approximately 3 to 4 grams. If we take an average of 3.5 grams, the total seed weight is 133,333 × 3.5 grams = 466,665 grams, or approximately <strong>466 kilograms</strong>. This is an ideal number. In practice, always add 5 to 10 percent to account for loss or seed damage due to field unevenness. Thus, the garlic seed amount per hectare can range from <strong>470 to 520 kilograms</strong> .</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-سیر-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقدار بذر سیر در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare for Garlic</figcaption></figure><h3>Impact of drip irrigation on planting space</h3><p>Use of <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%86%d8%ad%d9%88%d9%87-%d8%a7%d9%86%d8%aa%d8%ae%d8%a7%d8%a8-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a2%d8%a8%db%8c%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c-%d9%82%d8%b7%d8%b1%d9%87-%d8%a7%db%8c-%d9%85%d9%86%d8%a7%d8%b3%d8%a8/" title="نحوه انتخاب نوار آبیاری قطره ای مناسب">Appropriate drip irrigation tapes</a> allow you to consider slightly narrower row spacing because roots have better access to water. However, the key point is that the tape line must be placed exactly in the middle between two rows to reduce competition between roots for water. You can read the article <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%B4%D9%86%D8%A8%D9%84%DB%8C%D9%84%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/" title="مقدار بذر شنبلیله در هکتار">Fennel Seed Calculation Guide</a> as well, since the logic of seed density there is similar.</p><><h2>Practical tips for seed purchasing and preparation</h2><p>When buying garlic seed cloves, check for health and firmness. Soft or bruised cloves should not be planted. To improve planting accuracy, you can use garlic planters that maintain consistent spacing. If using a manual method, pulling a string to mark rows helps keep 15 cm spacing.</p><h3>Water and Nutrient Management</h3><ul><li>Garlic seeds require high soil moisture, but fluctuating moisture levels can cause cloves to split. Using precision irrigation systems helps maintain a stable root zone environment.</li><li>Mulching can reduce weed growth and conserve soil moisture, reducing the need for frequent irrigation.</li><li>For information on the benefits of modern systems, refer to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/foidai-norabiyari-tip/" title="فواید نوار آبیاری تیپ">Drip Line Advantages</a> a guide that shows how this technology can optimize the performance of small-sized crops like garlic.</li></ul><h2>Different Levels of Density and Performance</h2><p>Some farmers plant specific garlic varieties at higher densities. The table below provides a quick comparison of different densities:</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-سیر-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر سیر در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare, garlic crop</figcaption></figure><table><thead><tr><th>Row spacing (m)</th><th>Plant spacing (m)</th><th>Number of cloves per hectare</th><th>Estimated seed weight (kg)</th><th>Remarks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0.15</td><td>0.05</td><td>133,333</td><td>466 - 520</td><td>Standard for medium colza</td></tr><tr><td>0.20</td><td>0.05</td><td>100,000</td><td>350 - 400</td><td>Suitable for large-cluster varieties</td></tr><tr><td>0.15</td><td>0.04</td><td>166,666</td><td>583 - 650</td><td>High density, requires more moisture</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Remember that these figures are approximate and vary depending on your seed and soil conditions. For more detailed information on selecting an irrigation system compatible with these densities, you can <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/comprehensive-irrigation-tape-greenhouse-guide-0-to-100/" title="راهنمای جامع نوار آبیاری گلخانه">Comprehensive Guide to Greenhouse Drip Irrigation</a> Study this, as the physical principles of flow in strips are the same.</p><><h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><h3>1. Is the garlic seed rate per hectare fixed?</h3><p>No, it is not fixed. This amount depends on variety size, planting distance, and soil type. Large-cloved varieties require more space, while small-cloved varieties have higher density.</p><h3>2. What is the best time to plant garlic seed?</h3><p>It is usually planted in early autumn (Aban or Azar months) so that the bulbs have sufficient time to fill and thicken during winter and spring.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-سیر-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر سیر در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Garlic crop seed rate per hectare</figcaption></figure><h3>3. Can drip irrigation be used for garlic?</h3><p>Yes, drip irrigation is one of the best methods for garlic because it controls root zone moisture and prevents bulb rot caused by prolonged wetness. To learn more, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/perforated-drip-tape-irrigation/" title="آبیاری نوار سوراخ دار قطره ای">Punched drip tape irrigation guide</a> review this resource, which provides good technical details about various types of tape.</p><h2>Summary</h2><p>Precise calculation <strong>Garlic seed quantity per hectare</strong> is a scientific process that is predictable by considering planting distances and variety weights. Under standard conditions, approximately 450 to 500 kg of seed is recommended per hectare. To ensure success, we recommend using suitable irrigation systems and paying attention to the quality of the purchased seed. By adhering to planting distance principles and water management, you can achieve excellent yields from your garlic crop.</p>','Garlic Seed Quantity Per Hectare: Comprehensive Guide for Farmers','This article covers formulas for calculating garlic seed quantities per hectare, optimal planting spacings, and the impact of drip irrigation systems on clover growth. A comprehensive and practical guide for farmers.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
