INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Critical Importance of Drip Line Layout in Lentil Fields</h2>\n<p>Lentil is one of the key legumes in Iranian agriculture that, due to its relative sensitivity to water and soil management, requires particular care in the design of irrigation systems. One of the most important technical parameters that farmers should be familiar with is <strong>the drip line spacing in lentil cropping</strong> . This spacing directly relates to the planting pattern, root development depth, and evaporation from the soil surface. Incorrect spacing between rows and drip lines can lead to root water stress, asymmetric plant growth, and ultimately a reduction in final yield.</p>\n<p>In this article, we examine the technical details of lentil Row Layout and the placement of drip lines within this system. Our aim is to provide a practical guide to help farmers make the best decisions based on their local climate and soil conditions. Familiarity with the principles of <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/type-irrigation-tape-installation-method/">drip line installation methods</a> in other crops can also provide complementary insights for a better understanding of the challenges specific to lentil.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Technical Analysis of Planting Patterns and Root Development in Lentils</h2>\n<p>To determine the appropriate tape spacing, the root anatomy of lentil must first be considered. Lentil roots are shallow; approximately 70 to 80 percent of the root mass is located within the top 30 centimeters of soil. Therefore, the drip tape must be placed precisely at this ring depth. If the row spacing is too wide, dry zones will form between adjacent roots even if the tape is attached to each row, causing plant stress during peak air temperatures.</p>\n<h3>Golden Standards for Row Spacing</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Broadcast Seed Sowing:</strong> Usually, the use of drip tape is more difficult in this method due to the irregular distribution of roots, and tapes are often installed in rows (e.g., every 40 centimeters).</li>\n<li><strong>Row Sowing with Layout:</strong> The optimal condition for lentil is a row spacing of 45 to 60 centimeters. In this case, it is recommended to use one central drip tape between two rows or two drip tapes adhered to the bottom of planting cups.</li>\n<li><strong>Impact on Density:</strong> Increasing plant density per square meter requires shorter spacing between tapes to activate the full growth potential of soil coverage.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>When reviewing the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/qadamhoi-nasbi-navori-tip/">stages of drip tape installation,</a> we find that the mechanical stability of the tape throughout the growing season, particularly during seed drilling at sowing, is of high importance. Chickpea, due to its small seed size, can present a specific challenge for seed clamps in some precision seeding systems; therefore, the distance of the drip tape from the sowing line (typically 10 to 15 centimeters laterally) must be set so that it does not interfere with sowing mechanization.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-عدس-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت عدس: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop chickpea</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Effect of drip tape spacing on pathology and root diseases</h2>\n<p>One of the hidden factors in drip tape spacing for chickpea is moisture management and the prevention of rotting diseases. Root Rot in conditions of over-irrigation with tapes spaced far apart and at incorrect flow rates is common. Chickpea is sensitive to water accumulation in the root zone. If parallel tapes are spaced too closely, in clay soils moisture permeability to deeper layers is slow, and moisture accumulates in the lateral tapes.</p>\n<h3>Recommended layout pattern for heavy and light soils</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Light and sandy soils:</strong> In these soils, vertical irrigation infiltration is rapid. It is recommended to use strips with a row spacing of 50 cm and an appropriate flow rate. A \'double row\' layout with a central strip between each two rows provides very high efficiency in these soils.</li>\n<li><strong>Clay and heavy soils:</strong> Under these conditions, there is a risk of waterlogging in the strip. It is better to slightly increase the distance between planting lines (up to 65 cm) and place strip emitters, rather than straight lines, in wider strips so that a sharp wetting front does not form and penetrate into deeper layers.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Similar irrigation behavior in other vegetables can also be helpful; for example, in <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d8%aa%d8%b1%d9%87-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Leafy and vegetable crops</a> which have shallow roots, the principles of strip emitter spacing are very similar to those for lentils. In both cases, the main goal is complete coverage of the active root zone without creating moisture pockets.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Practical tips for optimizing strip emitter spacing</h2>\n<p>Field implementation is sometimes accompanied by on-ground challenges. The following are the most important practical points for lentil farmers:</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-عدس-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت عدس: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing, row layout, crop: lentil</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Balance between cost and yield</h3>\n<p>The further apart the tapes are spaced, the less tape is required per hectare, reducing installation overhead. However, this cost reduction may be offset by an irrecoverable yield decrease of 20 to 30 percent. In <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%da%a9%d8%af%d9%88-%d8%a2%d8%ac%db%8c%d9%84%db%8c-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">studies related to squash and vegetable cultivation</a> it has also been observed that optimizing tape spacing identifies the optimal point between vegetable costs and final yield. For lentils, it is recommended to use the pattern of “two parallel tapes with 45 cm spacing” as a starting baseline.</p>\n<h3>Monitoring tape planting depth</h3>\n<p>Tape lateral spacing is not the only variable; planting depth also plays a role. If the drip tape is placed on the soil surface, moisture evaporation and tape decay due to mice and insects increase. The drip tape should be placed at a soil depth of 10 to 15 centimeters, which aligns with the main root nodes of lentils.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>1. Can we use a central drip tape strip between rows instead of placing it against the roots?</h3>\n<p>Yes, for row spacings greater than 60 cm, placing a central strip may be logical. However, for standard spacings of 45 to 50 cm, placing the strip against each row or using double strips provides better root coverage.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-عدس-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت عدس: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop lentil</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>2. What is the role of soil type in adjusting strip spacing?</h3>\n<p>In clay soils, spacings should be slightly wider (55–65 cm) so that moisture reaches the roots quickly and waterlogging does not occur. In sandy soils, spacings can be tighter (45–50 cm) because roots spread more extensively to access water.</p>\n<h3>3. Is drip tape spacing related to water scarcity in the region?</h3>\n<p>In arid regions, using closer spacings between strips creates a continuous moisture zone around the roots, increasing water use efficiency. However, an economic analysis must be conducted considering the investment cost.</p>\n\n<h2>Summary and Conclusion</h2>\n<p>Topic <strong>Drip line spacing for lentil cultivation</strong> It is a site-specific measured parameter that depends on multiple factors. However, in general, maintaining a row spacing of 45 to 60 centimeters, along with the correct installation of the drip tape at the active root depth, can lead to a significant increase in seed quality and a reduction in water usage. The most successful farmers are those who accurately adapt the \'double row\' or \'central strip\' pattern to their local soil type and climate through local trial and error. With complementary studies such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/mikorit-khomi-yufa-hamadoni-dar-hektar/">use of mycorrhiza on the plant</a> and planting density control, the full potential of drip irrigation systems for lentils can be exploited.</p>','Tip Line Spacing in Lentil Cropping: Recommended Standards','Selecting the appropriate drip tape spacing for lentil crops directly impacts root rot, economic yield, and water management. In this article from navar-abyari.ir, we review the gold standards for row layout and drip tape installation.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
