SET @slug_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name='tape-drip-irrigation-maintenance-soybean-cultivation' AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
SET @resolved_slug=IF(@slug_conflict IS NULL,'tape-drip-irrigation-maintenance-soybean-cultivation','tape-drip-irrigation-maintenance-soybean-cultivation-crop-242-en');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
SET @resolved_slug=IF(@resolved_conflict IS NULL,@resolved_slug,'tape-drip-irrigation-maintenance-soybean-cultivation-crop-242-en-351affbc');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction to the importance of maintaining tiepe tape in soybean cultivation</h2>\n<p>Soybean is one of the most important oilseed and protein crops in the world and has high sensitivity to irrigation conditions. The use of drip irrigation systems, particularly <strong>tiepe tape</strong> (Tiepe Tape), is considered an ideal method for modern farmers due to its high water-use efficiency and uniform distribution. However, this technology is not complete with correct installation alone; it also requires precise planning and <strong>regular maintenance</strong> . Many farmers believe that after planting, the irrigation system operates automatically, but the reality is that clogging of dripper holes, tape degradation, or improper placement next to plants can cause a significant reduction in yield.</p>\n<p>In this article, we examine in detail the key maintenance points for tiepe tape specifically in soybean farms. Our goal is to provide practical guidance so that farmers can achieve the highest efficiency from this irrigation system with minimal cost. Paying attention to fine details from pre-planting to the end of the growing period guarantees plant health and seed quality.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Specific characteristics of soybean and its irrigation requirements</h2>\n<h3>Rooting and root distribution in sand</h3>\n<p>Soybean is a crop with a deep and lateral root system. In the first weeks after planting, young roots are very delicate and require gentle, balanced irrigation. Drip tape, if installed at a distance of 10 to 15 cm from the planting row, controls water penetration depth and prevents surface drying. In contrast, rainfall irrigation may cause soil compaction and reduce oxygen supply to the roots.</p>\n<h3>Sensitivity to water stress and phloem</h3>\n<p>Soybean is most sensitive to irrigation during the pod setting stage (R3 to R6). Water deficit at this stage directly affects seed weight. The drip tape system, by providing a stable water flow with controlled discharge, allows the plant to continue growing under less stress. Therefore, ensuring that the tape is not blocked during this phase is vital.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-سویا-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="نگهداری سویا با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care soybean</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Key points for drip tape maintenance: Before the start of the irrigation season</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Complete visual inspection:</strong> Before each irrigation season, remove previous tapes and inspect them for tears, kinks, or color changes (especially darkening, which indicates sediment accumulation).</li>\n  <li><strong>Use of appropriate filters:</strong> Installing a disk or screen filter with a 120 mesh or finer mesh prevents suspended particles from entering the micro-holes of the drip line. Ensure that the input water pressure to the line does not exceed the limit specified in the technical specifications.</li>\n  <li><strong>System pressure control:</strong> Excessive pressure increases flow velocity and the likelihood of the line deviating from the row. The use of a pressure regulator at the beginning of each line is recommended.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For a better understanding of standards related to measurement and installation, you can read the article on eggplant seed quantity per hectare + planting and irrigation tips, as the general principles of row irrigation align with it. Additionally, understanding salin seed quantity per hectare can help you adjust planting density to the discharge capacity of the drip line.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Practical care tips during the soybean growth period</h2>\n<h3>Germination (Sprouting) and the seedling stage</h3>\n<p>At this stage, soybean seeds are located at a depth of 5 to 10 centimeters. The drip line must be installed so that water does not spray directly onto the soil surface but penetrates below it. Be careful that the drip tape does not tangle with the seed during planting. Using lines with a flow rate of 4 to 6 liters per hour is ideal at this stage. If you are using an old pump system, ensure that <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%86%DA%AF%D9%87%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D9%88-%D9%85%D8%AF%DB%8C%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A2%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D8%AA%DB%8C%D9%BE/">Drip Tape Irrigation Maintenance and Management</a> Ensure that the holes are clear.</p>\n<h3>Covering and Branching Stage</h3>\n<p>As soybean plants grow, leaves cover the drip tape. This helps retain soil moisture but prevents flushing and cleaning the tape at the end of the season. At this point, if you compare the drip tape spacing in similar crops, you will notice that similar principles apply. For comparison, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%81%d8%a7%d8%b5%d9%84%d9%87-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%84%d9%88%d8%a8%db%8c%d8%a7/">Drip tape spacing in beans</a> can serve as a model for your mechanical settings in soybean, as both plants are legumes with similar root requirements.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-سویا-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="نگهداری سویا با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care soybean</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Comparative Table of Soybean Irrigation Needs at Different Stages with Drip Tape Settings</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Soybean growth stage</th>\n      <th>Water demand breakdown (L/ha)</th>\n      <th>Recommended drip line settings</th>\n      <th>Special maintenance attention</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Budding (R1)</td>\n      <td>50 - 60</td>\n      <td>Flow rate 4 L/h, interval 4–5 hours</td>\n      <td>Check cleanliness of liquid filters</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Full canopy cover (R2–R3)</td>\n      <td>60 - 80</td>\n      <td>Flow rate 6 liters/hour, duration 6-7 hours</td>\n      <td>Monitor inlet pressure to the system</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Grain filling (R4-R6)</td>\n      <td>80 - 100</td>\n      <td>Flow rate 8 liters/hour, duration 8-10 hours</td>\n      <td>Inspect mini connectors for leaks</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>Note that these figures are estimates and must be adjusted based on soil type (loam, clay, or sandy) and regional climate. Heavier soils require less frequent applications with higher water volumes per irrigation event, while lighter soils require more frequent applications with lower volumes. In this regard, studying factors affecting the performance of other crops such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/barley-yield-per-hectare-factors-increase/">barley yield per hectare factors increase</a> can provide a broader perspective on water resource management in cereal and legume cropping systems.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Post-harvest: Final maintenance and preparation for the next season</h2>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Purging:</strong> Before collecting the drip tape, increase the water pressure to the maximum allowable limit and run the system for 15 minutes without the tape (or with the tape unrolled) to flush out clay deposits and organic matter.</li>\n  <li><strong>Correct collection:</strong> Roll the tapes into small rolls (5 to 10 meters in length) and place them in special bags or shaded boxes. Exposing them to direct sunlight causes damage to the tape polymer.</li>\n  <li><strong>Inspection and damage assessment:</strong> Randomly open approximately 10% of the tapes and inspect the dripper orifices with a magnifying glass. If blockages are observed, discard the tape; repairing the orifices of a single drip tape is practically as costly and risky as manufacturing a new tape.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>Is drip tape suitable for soybeans with a row spacing of 60 cm?</h3>\n<p>Yes, one drip tape line per row is recommended, placed 15 cm away from the center of the row. This distance keeps the roots moist without coming into direct contact with the stem.</p>\n<h3>When should the drip tape be replaced?</h3>\n<p>Drip tape typically has a useful lifespan of two to three seasons. If, after seasonal flushing, the flow through the holes becomes uneven or the tape looks clearer and thinner, replace it. Using worn-out tape leads to uneven irrigation and increased weed spread.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-سویا-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="نگهداری سویا با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care soybean</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Can drip tape also be used for crop fertilization (Fertigation)?</h3>\n<p>Yes, but you must exercise great caution. Nutrients must be completely water-soluble and pass through dual filters. Deposits of insoluble materials cause permanent clogging of the tape. Always flush the system with pure water before each fertilization injection.</p>\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>Maintaining drip tape in soybean crops is a continuous process, from installation to the end of subsequent seasons. A drip tape irrigation system only yields maximum returns when hygiene, filtration, and pressure management are consciously handled. By following the above guidelines, you can ensure that every drop of water is effectively delivered to your soybean roots and achieve sustainable performance in future years. Sustainable farming, as discussed in related articles like <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/pumpkin-seed-per-hectare-factors/">pumpkin seed per hectare factors</a> As can be seen, it stems from the precise management of natural resources.</p>','Tape Drip Irrigation Maintenance for Soybean Cultivation: Key and Practical Tips','A practical article on the proper maintenance of drip lines in soybean cultivation, aimed at improving irrigation efficiency and reducing farming costs.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
