SET @resolved_slug=IF(@resolved_conflict IS NULL,@resolved_slug,'technical-specs-125mm-riser-pipe-selection-guide-prod-082-en-bd4ca235');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Importance of Selecting 125 mm Threaded Pipes Correctly</h2>\n<p>In drip and line irrigation systems, 125 mm threaded pipes function not only as the main water carrier but also as the vital artery distributing pressure throughout the network. Many farmers, when purchasing pipes, focus solely on price and neglect critical technical parameters such as material durability, UV resistance, and compatibility with operating pressure. Pipes with a diameter of 125 mm are typically used in the main or secondary lines of medium to large farms, managing higher flow rates compared to 75 or 100 mm pipes.</p>\n<p>The use of low-quality 125 mm threaded pipes can lead to a significant drop in pressure at the end of line irrigation lines. This causes some field areas to remain dry while others suffer from over-irrigation, resulting in reduced crop yield and quality. To better understand how proper irrigation impacts productivity, you can refer to the guide on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/mikdori-tukhmi-arzi-dar-yek-hektar-rahnamoi-mukammal/">Arecal Yield in One Hectare: A Complete Guide</a> which demonstrates how precise resource management affects final output.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Key Technical Specifications of 125 mm Threaded Pipes</h2>\n<h3>Pipe Body Material and Structure</h3>\n<p>Most 125 mm threaded pipes available on the market are made of polyethylene (PE) with various LDPE or LLDPE grades. Selecting the appropriate material directly affects the pipe\'s useful life. High-quality pipes feature a UV-resistant coating that prevents chemical degradation under direct sunlight. Pipes lacking this protection become dry and brittle after one summer season and are prone to leaks in the following season.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مشخصات-فنی-لوله-نخدار-125-میلیمتر-راهنمای-انتخاب-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مشخصات فنی لوله نخدار 125 میلیمتر: راهنمای انتخاب - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>Selection of technical specifications for 125 mm threaded pipe product</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Working pressure and burst pressure</h3>\n<p>One of the most important technical specifications is the maximum working pressure (Max Working Pressure). 125 mm threaded pipes are generally designed for medium to low-pressure systems. You must ensure that the pipe\'s design pressure matches the output pressure of the farm\'s main pump. If the pump pressure exceeds the pipe\'s allowable pressure, the pipe should be selected as steel-wire reinforced or multi-layer PE to prevent sudden bursting.</p>\n<h3>Inner diameter and allowable flow rate</h3>\n<p>Despite the 125 mm designation, the exact inner diameter (ID) in millimeters must be specified by the manufacturer, as pipe wall thickness affects this value. The allowable flow rate for 125 mm threaded pipes is determined based on flow velocity. To maintain flow uniformity in drip tape lines, the flow velocity within the pipe should not exceed technical limits; otherwise, pressure loss along the pipe will increase.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for installation and connection to drip tape</h2>\n<h3>Proper connection using perforated fittings</h3>\n<p>When connecting 125 mm threaded pipes to lateral taps, it is essential to use high-quality metal or plastic collectors. Leaks at connection points are the main enemy of drip tape systems. Copper nuts and EPDM washers with long service life should be used. Additionally, the pipe should be placed in connection housings with at least 10% to 15% extra length to allow for adjustment in case relocation is required.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مشخصات-فنی-لوله-نخدار-125-میلیمتر-راهنمای-انتخاب-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مشخصات فنی لوله نخدار 125 میلیمتر: راهنمای انتخاب - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Product technical specs selection Threaded pipe 125 millimeters</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Impact of Threaded pipe 125 millimeters on crop performance</h3>\n<p>Selecting the main pipe size directly affects the flow rate received by each meter of drip line. In uniform crops such as forage corn, precise flow calculations are critical. If Threaded pipe 125 millimeters with an inappropriate flow rate is selected, water distribution will be asymmetric. To understand the importance of uniform water distribution in corn crops, review the guide for <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/corn-drip-tape-spacing-forage-corn-guide/">Drip line spacing for forage corn</a> recommended, which demonstrates how line layout coordinates with main pipe selection.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Selection strategy based on crop type and farm</h2>\n<h3>Matching cropping patterns</h3>\n<p>Farms with rotational cropping patterns require pipes that offer high flexibility in installation and re-layout. Threaded pipe 125 millimeters has less flexibility compared to extra-ordinary pipes due to its larger diameter; therefore, in large farms, more collectors are required to ensure the pipe runs straight without severe bends.</p>\n<h3>Impact on grain crops</h3>\n<p>In crops such as irrigated barley, water management over short planting intervals is highly sensitive. If a 125 mm threaded pipe is correctly selected, it ensures that pressure remains constant throughout the drip line. This pressure stability is essential for maintaining uniform germination rates across all planting plots. In this regard, understanding the factors affecting <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d8%ac%d9%88-%d8%a2%d8%a8%db%8c-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">The quantity of irrigated barley seed per hectare</a> helps in better estimating the water requirements based on seed density and selecting the appropriate pipe size.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مشخصات-فنی-لوله-نخدار-125-میلیمتر-راهنمای-انتخاب-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مشخصات فنی لوله نخدار 125 میلیمتر: راهنمای انتخاب - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product technical specs selection 125 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Is the 125 mm threaded pipe recyclable?</strong><br>Yes, PE pipes are recyclable. However, economically, they are usually replaced after 5 to 10 years of use due to mechanical and chemical wear.</li>\n<li><strong>When should a 125 mm pipe be used instead of a 100 mm pipe?</strong><br>A 125 mm threaded pipe is the better choice when the total system flow in a straight line requires transferring more than approximately 200 to 250 liters per minute, or when the length of the branch lines is very long and pressure drop must be minimized.</li>\n<li><strong>Is a 125 mm threaded pipe suitable for greenhouses?</strong><br>Typically, smaller pipes (such as 25 to 50 mm) are used in greenhouses, unless the greenhouse system is very large and requires a main transfer pipe; in that case, a 125 mm threaded pipe is appropriate.</li>\n<li><strong>What is the role of gasket material in pipe longevity?</strong><br>EPDM rubber gaskets must be resistant to pressure and UV. Using low-quality gaskets leads to leaks and gradual pressure drop over time, which in turn disrupts drip line performance.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<h2>Conclusion and Final Recommendation</h2>\n<p>Choosing a 125 mm threaded pipe is a technical decision that must be made based on precise hydraulic calculations, soil type, cropping pattern, and available system pressure. Simply purchasing a cheaper pipe can be more costly due to early replacement and water losses than buying a high-quality pipe. It is recommended to consult an irrigation engineer before purchase to verify the size and wall thickness of the 125 mm threaded pipe based on the existing farm pump and line lengths.</p>\n<p>Additionally, it is crucial to consider crop-specific variables in irrigation calculations. For instance, if tomatoes are part of your crop, precise fluctuations in water pressure directly affect fruit growth. Studies <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/increase-tomato-yield-per-hectare-iraq-farmers-guide/">guiding the increase of tomatoes per hectare</a> indicate that the intelligent management of pipeline pressure can be a key factor in improving the final yield. Ultimately, a successful irrigation system is one where the pipeline, drip line, and crop operate simultaneously and in coordination.</p>','Technical Specifications of 125mm Riser Pipe: Selection Guide','Selecting the appropriate 125 mm threaded pipe is key to maintaining consistent pressure along pipeline lines and optimizing drip tape performance. This guide explains the critical technical parameters for engineers and farmers.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
