SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2> Introduction: The Importance of Selecting the Right Pipe in Drip Irrigation</h2><p>Proper selection of irrigation system components, particularly main and sub-main pipes, plays a critical role in farm efficiency and sustainability. Threaded pipes, due to their quick connection capability and high flexibility, are a popular option in irrigation networks. In this context, <strong>75 mm threaded pipe</strong> has attracted the attention of many farmers and specialists because of its widespread use in main lines and distribution. However, the main question is: What distinguishes the 75 mm pipe from other brands?</p><p>Below, through a detailed technical analysis, we compare products based on material quality, durability under environmental conditions, and installation capabilities to examine their differences and similarities. The goal is to make informed decisions by better understanding the features of each brand. For a better understanding of the overall system layout, you can read the article on drip irrigation system components with tape type to gain a comprehensive view of the pipe\'s role in the entire system.</p><p>  </p><h2> Technical and Structural Features of 75 mm Threaded Pipe</h2><h3> Polyethylene Material and Resin Quality</h3><p>The most important factor distinguishing different brands is the type of polymer used in pipe manufacturing. Standard pipes use medium density polyethylene (MDPE) or high density polyethylene (HDPE). Reputable brands use high-purity grade resins that ensure higher chemical and mechanical resistance. Low-quality pipes may use recycled resins, which significantly reduces their useful life when exposed to UV radiation and temperature fluctuations.</p><h3> Wall thickness and internal ribs</h3><p>The 75 mm threaded pipe, in addition to the smooth pipe, features internal ribs that increase surface contact area and resistance to lateral pull-out. When comparing brands, attention should be paid to the depth and consistency of these ribs. Brands utilizing advanced injection molding technology produce more uniform and robust ribs. This feature is critical for main lines that withstand higher pressures. For selecting the appropriate wall thickness based on product type, the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/optimal-wall-thickness-tip-irrigation-tape/">optimal wall thickness guide for drip tape</a> can provide adequate insight, as similar mechanical principles govern the selection of main line pipe thickness as well.</p><h2> Comparison with other and domestic brands</h2><h3> Imported brands vs. Iranian brands</h3><p>The Iranian market witnesses the presence of multiple brands, including European, Chinese, and Iranian ones. European brands generally score higher in terms of safety factor and UV resistance but are expensive. Chinese brands offer high variety and competitive pricing, but their quality is variable and requires detailed inspection of standard certifications (CE or ISO). Iranian brands, relying on the localization of raw materials and an understanding of Iran\'s climatic conditions, offer logical and cost-effective options.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقایسه-لوله-نخ-دار-75-میلیمتر-با-سایر-برندها-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقایسه لوله نخ دار 75 میلیمتر با سایر برندها - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>product comparison brand features 75 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><p>For a more detailed comparison, the table below shows the key features:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Feature </th><th> Brand A (Imported) </th><th> Brand B (Iranian) </th><th> Brand C (Chinese) </th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Tensile strength </td><td> Very high </td><td> High </td><td> Medium </td></tr><tr><td> UV Resistance </td><td> 10 years </td><td> 8 years </td><td> 5 years </td></tr><tr><td> Thread Size Accuracy </td><td> Metric </td><td> Metric </td><td> Potential deviation </td></tr><tr><td> Relative price </td><td> High </td><td> Medium </td><td> Low </td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ultimately, choosing between brands depends on your budget and expected lifespan. If you are looking for a system that lasts for years without replacement, paying a higher upfront cost is logical. However, for short-term projects, mid-range brands are also viable. Understanding the principles of deficit irrigation, including its features and drawbacks, can also influence the selection of the main system, as the type of irrigation determines the required pipe pressure.</p><p>  </p><h2> Practical tips for installing and connecting 75 mm pipes</h2><h3> Importance of using Cap Card</h3><p>The biggest issue when installing threaded pipes is leakage at the joints. Using a standard seal collar appropriate for the pipe thickness is essential. Some manufacturers produce proprietary seal collars that may not be compatible with couplings from other brands. Therefore, when purchasing 75 mm pipes, ensure that the fittings are compatible with the couplings you have available. Leakage in main lines can lead to water loss and reduced pressure at the end of the line.</p><h3> Layout and Allowable Bending</h3><p>75 mm pipes have good flexibility, but sharp bends can cause deformation of the threads and reduced flow rate. In main line design, avoid bends with a small radius. The pipe path should be routed to avoid rocky or sharp areas. Additionally, the pipe must be laid on an appropriate bed to prevent contact with the ground in areas with deep ruts. Familiarization with <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/nuqtahoi-muhim-hangomi-istifodai-lundahoi-tipisi-baroi-obyori/">Key points when using tape pipes for irrigation</a>, even if it is a main pipe, similar principles apply to flow management.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقایسه-لوله-نخ-دار-75-میلیمتر-با-سایر-برندها-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقایسه لوله نخ دار 75 میلیمتر با سایر برندها - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Product comparison brand features threaded pipe 75 mm</figcaption></figure><h3> Working pressure and Sagging Risks</h3><p>Due to the presence of threads, threaded pipes offer higher tensile strength compared to smooth pipes, but they remain sensitive to internal pressure. During startup, increase the pressure gradually to prevent sudden bursts at weak points. Also, in cold seasons, water accumulation in the pipe and freezing can cause increased pressure and pipe rupture. Draining the pipe after irrigation is complete is a critical step.</p><h2> Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><h3> Is a 75 mm pipe suitable for lateral lines?</h3><p>Generally, 75 mm pipes are designed for main lines and primary distribution. For lateral lines directly feeding drip tape or drip lines, 50 mm or 40 mm sizes typically offer better performance. Using larger pipes for laterals reduces flow velocity and fails to ensure uniform distribution, unless the lateral length is very long.</p><h3> How can I verify brand authenticity?</h3><p>Always look for standard certification labels, the manufacturer\'s name, UV symbols, and production dates on the pipes. Reputable brands use a unique code for each pipe roll. Additionally, purchasing from authorized dealers or official distributors reduces the risk of buying counterfeit products. While learning about other system components, such as the article on seed rate per hectare, may not have a direct connection, it demonstrates the technical precision required; this same attention to detail must be applied when selecting pipes.</p><h3> Can a 75 mm pipe be repaired?</h3><p>No, polyethylene pipes such as 75 mm are generally not suitable for heat fusion or soldering, especially those with internal threads. In the event of a burst or damage, the only solution is to remove and replace the damaged section. Therefore, pipe durability is a determining factor for your operational costs.</p><h2> Conclusion and Final Recommendations</h2><p>Selection <strong>75 mm threaded pipe</strong> Correctly, it combines technical knowledge, budget, and an understanding of farm needs. Different brands each have their advantages and disadvantages: European brands offer the best quality at a higher price, Iranian brands provide a good balance between price and quality, and Chinese brands are options for projects with tighter budgets. The most important point is purchasing pipes that meet real standards and using fittings properly.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقایسه-لوله-نخ-دار-75-میلیمتر-با-سایر-برندها-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقایسه لوله نخ دار 75 میلیمتر با سایر برندها - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product comparison brand features 75 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><p>To increase efficiency, design the irrigation system based on the plant\'s root requirements. Instead of focusing solely on the pipe, consider the entire system. You can ensure that the pump\'s output pressure matches the pipe and other components\' pressure limits by reviewing the drip tape water pressure measurement guide. Ultimately, regular system maintenance and monitoring is the key to the longevity of your investment.</p><p>  </p><p> We hope this comparison will clarify your perspective for your next purchase. Always prioritize quality over quantity, as the cost of replacing a broken pipe is far greater than the price difference between high-quality pipes.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%a2%d8%a8%db%8c%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c-%d8%ae%d8%b1%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%a8%db%8c-%da%86%db%8c%d8%b3%d8%aa%d8%9f-%d9%88%db%8c%da%98%da%af%db%8c-%d9%87%d8%a7-%d9%88-%d9%85%d8%b9%d8%a7%db%8c%d8%a8/">What is deficit irrigation? Characteristics and disadvantages</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%b7-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d9%8a-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%aa%d9%86%d9%82%d9%8a%d8%b7-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d8%b1%d8%a8%d9%8a%d9%84/">Drip Irrigation Line in Erbil: The Comprehensive Guide to Modern Farming</a></p>','In-Depth Review of 75mm Ribbed Pipe vs. Competing Brands','In this article, we conduct a detailed review of the 75 mm threaded pipe and compare it with other brands available in the market to help you make the best choice for your irrigation system.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
