SET @resolved_slug=IF(@resolved_conflict IS NULL,@resolved_slug,'110mm-ribbed-irrigation-pipe-buyers-guide-prod-103-en-66a1618b');
SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Importance of 110mm Male-Threaded Pipes in Modern Irrigation</h2><p>In precision irrigation systems, particularly drip and tape irrigation, the proper selection of main transfer pipes plays a critical role in system efficiency. The 110mm male-threaded water pipe is a popular choice for farmers and civil engineering projects due to its standard diameter and butt-fusion connection. However, purchasing this product without understanding its pressure rating, polymer material, and manufacturing standards can lead to costly damage such as leaks, cracking, and reduced system lifespan. In this article, we provide a specialized, non-promotional guide to the selection criteria, flow rate calculation methods, and practical tips required for a secure purchase. Our goal is to enable you to make fully informed decisions that reduce long-term costs and optimize crop yield. Given the variety of brands and samples available in the market, having a predefined checklist to assess the physical and chemical quality of pipes is essential. This guide is specifically designed to eliminate market confusion and steer you toward a smart selection.</p>\n<h2>Detailed Understanding of 110mm Male-Threaded Pipes: Technical Features</h2><p>110 mm pipes are typically manufactured from polyethylene (PE) with specific thermal properties. The threaded or press-fit feature of these pipes enables quick and secure connections to metal or polymer fittings. Compared to thermal welding, these connections are demountable, which is highly practical for future maintenance or pipeline modifications. A key selection criterion is the PN (Nominal Pressure) rating. For medium-pressure main water lines, PN10 to PN16 are generally used, while higher-pressure lines require PN16 or above. Understanding these concepts is the first step in preventing early pipe failure during high-pressure seasons. Additionally, knowing how threaded pipes react to varying atmospheric and ground pressures helps in better predicting the system\'s service life. Many novice farmers overlook these details, although they are decisive for the longevity of the irrigation system.</p>\n<h3>Visual specifications and precise measurement</h3><ul><li><strong>Outside diameter (OD):</strong> 110 mm. The diameter must be measured using calipers to eliminate manufacturing errors. Even a 1 mm deviation from the standard can cause fitting issues.</li><li><strong>Wall thickness (SDR):</strong> The diameter-to-thickness ratio determines the working pressure. A lower SDR indicates greater thickness and higher working pressure. When purchasing, always compare the SDR chart with the PN rating to ensure compatibility.</li><li><strong>Color and UV:</strong> High-quality pipes have appropriate anti-UV properties to withstand solar radiation. If the pipe is exposed to direct sunlight, the presence of UV-resistant additives is critical, and you should inspect the pipe for any signs of degradation or peeling.</li></ul>\n<h2>Key Criteria for Selecting 110mm NPT Water Pipes</h2><p>To make an informed purchase, you must evaluate three main axes: application, pressure, and flow rate. These three elements form a triangle that must be firmly established to ensure your system\'s stability. Neglecting any of these factors can lead to premature replacement costs or reduced irrigation efficiency. Therefore, before entering the market and comparing prices, list these criteria and design your system accordingly.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-خرید-لوله-نخدار-110-میلیمتر-نکات-انتخاب-و-قیمت-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع خرید لوله نخدار 110 میلیمتر: نکات انتخاب و قیمت - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>Product Buying Guide: Selection and Price of 110mm NPT Pipes</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h3>Reviewing Required Pressure and Flow Rate</h3><p>Calculating the flow rate of your irrigation system is the first step. If you have selected a drip line system, as described on the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b9-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be/">Types of Drip Lines</a>page, the flow rate is generally lower, whereas drip lines with wider spacing require a higher flow rate. If you wish to learn more about the principles of selecting drip lines based on soil type and crop variety, read the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/payvasthoi-navori-tip-kishovarzi/">payvasthoi navori tip kishovarzi</a> article. In fact, the inlet pressure to the 110mm pipe must not exceed the PN rating of the selected pipe. The flow rate calculation process involves gathering data on the number of drippers, their spacing, and the uniformity coefficient. These calculations should be performed cautiously with a safety margin (e.g., 20%) to ensure that pressure in the pipe does not reach dangerous limits during hot days when water demand is higher. Additionally, land slope and transmission line length must be considered, as longer paths result in greater pressure loss, requiring a thicker pipe or a more powerful pump.</p>\n<h3>Pipe material and quality standards</h3><p>Always look for the Iranian National Standard or ISO logo. Unmarked pipes or those made from recycled material may crack during the first hot season. New PE100 or PE100-RC pipes offer higher tensile strength and a longer service life. When purchasing, inspect the pipe\'s surface; a standard pipe must have a smooth, uniform surface with no bubbles or irregular lines. Additionally, the embossed labels on the pipe body must be legible and include manufacturer information, standard, material, and wall thickness. Avoid purchasing pipes with faded labels or incomplete information, as this indicates poor quality or a counterfeit product. Furthermore, request laboratory certificates (such as pressure test reports) from the seller. Reputable sellers will proudly provide these documents, whereas dealers of substandard materials typically avoid submitting them.</p>\n\n<h2>Pricing evaluation of 110mm threaded pipes and influencing factors</h2><p>The price of 110mm water pipes fluctuates based on market conditions and is not fixed. Factors such as global polymer prices, transportation costs, and exchange rates affect the final price. Instead of relying on daily prices, which change rapidly, it is better to analyze based on \'price per meter\' and \'total installation cost\'. A cheaper pipe with a higher SDR (thinner wall) may require more repairs in the long term due to reduced working pressure, which is more costly than buying a higher-quality pipe. Therefore, calculating the ROI (Return on Investment) for each meter of pipe should include purchase costs, installation costs, maintenance costs, and potential repair costs over the pipe\'s useful life. This analysis helps you save money in the long term. Additionally, purchasing in bulk volumes can result in fairer tiered pricing and reduced logistical costs. If your project is large, be sure to compare prices from several different suppliers and include delivery terms and warranty conditions in your final calculation.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-خرید-لوله-نخدار-110-میلیمتر-نکات-انتخاب-و-قیمت-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع خرید لوله نخدار 110 میلیمتر: نکات انتخاب و قیمت - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Product buying guide selection price 110mm ribbed pipe</figcaption></figure><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Standard pipe</th><th>Industrial/Standard pipe</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Material</td><td>Compounded mix</td><td>Pure PE100</td></tr><tr><td>Wall thickness</td><td>Incompatible</td><td>Precise and standard</td></tr><tr><td>Warranty availability</td><td>Usually no</td><td>Yes (conditional on correct installation)</td></tr><tr><td>UV resistance</td><td>Low</td><td>Higher with additive</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Practical tips for installation and maintenance</h2><p>Proper installation of 110mm threaded pipes accounts for 50% of your system\'s lifespan. Avoid incomplete connections. When connecting to metal fittings, use appropriate PTFE washers to prevent leaks. Additionally, hole drilling for pipe passage must be done carefully to preserve the surrounding soil structure and prevent pipe sagging. To learn about additional drip irrigation tips, we recommend reviewing the article <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%AD%D9%84-%D9%86%D8%B5%D8%A8-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%AA%DB%8C%D9%BE/">Tape line installation steps</a> as well. This material will help you see the entire system in an integrated manner, not just individual pipe components. During installation, prevent scratches on the pipe body from sharp stones; if necessary, use sand pockets or rubber protectors. Additionally, wrap threaded connections with Teflon tape to prevent microscopic leaks that can grow into major leaks over time. After installation, flush the pipes with low-pressure water before connecting them to the main pump to remove foreign materials (such as soil), which helps prevent future clogging of emitters.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><ol><li><strong>Is 110mm pipe suitable for all drip systems?</strong><br>No. This diameter is suitable for higher flow rates or main lines. For sub-lines with low flow rates, 63mm or 50mm pipes may be sufficient. Using pipes larger than necessary causes water stagnation and sediment deposition, which reduces irrigation quality. Therefore, always remember to optimize the pipe diameter according to the required flow rate.</li><li><strong>How to Prevent Pipe Damage During Winter</strong><br>PE pipes are typically flexible, but if freezing liquids are present in the system, ice expansion can damage the fittings. Complete drainage of the system after the season ends is recommended. Additionally, storing the system and pumps in a closed, warm environment prevents freezing of metal components and damage to connections.</li></ol>\n<h2>Conclusion and Final Recommendations</h2><p>Buying 110mm threaded water pipes is a process where quality is more important than quantity. By considering the pressure rating, polymer material, and installation conditions, you can have an irrigation system that works without issues for years. Remember that an initial investment in main components such as pipes significantly reduces future repair and maintenance costs. To further optimize your performance, always pay attention to product data; for example, if you intend to grow tomatoes or similar crops, knowledge of green bean yield per hectare and the factors affecting it will help you calculate the required flow rate of the system more accurately and avoid overbuying or under-capacity. Precision irrigation is both an art and a science; use the right tools to achieve the desired result and transform your farm into a sustainable and profitable system.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-خرید-لوله-نخدار-110-میلیمتر-نکات-انتخاب-و-قیمت-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع خرید لوله نخدار 110 میلیمتر: نکات انتخاب و قیمت - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product buying guide selection price 110mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><p><strong>Related articles:</strong> Green bean yield per hectare + affecting factors, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/payvasthoi-navori-tip-kishovarzi/">payvasthoi navori tip kishovarzi</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%AD%D9%84-%D9%86%D8%B5%D8%A8-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%AA%DB%8C%D9%BE/">Drip line installation steps</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b9-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be/">Types of drip lines</a></p>\n<p><strong>Related content:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%d9%84%d9%88%d8%a8%db%8c%d8%a7-%d8%b3%d8%a8%d8%b2-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Green bean yield per hectare + influencing factors</a></p>','Comprehensive Guide to Buying 110mm Ribbed Irrigation Pipe: Selection and Price Factors','110 mm threaded pipes are the backbone of water conveyance systems in farms. This guide helps you select the best model while considering pressure, flow rate, and budget.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
