INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Importance of Selecting the Right Irrigation System</h2>\n<p>Selection <strong>Farm Irrigation System</strong> Choosing the appropriate irrigation system is one of the most critical decisions for farmers in ensuring economic yield and environmental sustainability. Given the constraints on water resources, utilizing low-consumption irrigation methods such as drip and subsurface band systems has transformed from a mere option into a strategic imperative. This article provides a comprehensive and practical guide to examining the nuances, advantages, and disadvantages of each method, as well as how to adapt them to specific farm conditions. This choice not only affects operational costs but also directly impacts the final product quality and the likelihood of successful sales in target markets.</p>\n<h2>Overview of Drip and Subsurface Band Irrigation Methods</h2>\n<p>Modern irrigation systems are based on the precise delivery of water and plant nutrients to the root zone. However, their flow dynamics and coverage patterns differ. Understanding these differences is the first step toward making an intelligent investment.</p>\n<h3>Drip Irrigation</h3>\n<p>In this method, water is applied drop by drop at very low flow rates directly to the root zone of the plant. This system is suitable for a variety of crops, including vegetables, fruit trees, and even small-grain crops such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%d8%ac%d9%88-%d8%a8%d9%87%d8%a7%d8%b1%d9%87-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Spring barley</a> and certain leafy green crops are suitable. The primary goal is to maintain permanent moisture in the root zone. Technically, emitters must have internal filters or be compatible with central filtration systems to prevent clogging of orifices.</p>\n<h3>Perforated tape irrigation</h3>\n<p>Perforated tape, also known as powder or dry tape, is a surface irrigation system where water flows as a narrow ribbon from one side to the other across the soil surface through a metal or plastic strip. This method is considered a surface-quantitative system, combining surface and drip irrigation. It is suitable for crops such as celery and some <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d8%a7%d8%b3%d9%81%d9%86%d8%a7%d8%ac-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Spinach</a> that require wider surface coverage, as it can be a better option. These systems typically have multiple and dense discharge zones, which allows water to be distributed more uniformly along the row.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-انتخاب-سیستم-آبیاری-برای-مزرعه-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع انتخاب سیستم آبیاری برای مزرعه - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p></p>\n<h2>Key criteria for selecting an irrigation system</h2>\n<p>For the final selection <strong>Farm irrigation system</strong>, it is essential to review the following parameters. Neglecting any of these factors can lead to premature equipment wear or reduced crop yield:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Crop type:</strong> Some crops such as tomato (pommé) use <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/pomidor-support-tape-guide/">supporting tape</a> and require precise point irrigation. In contrast, small-seed crops such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/shallot-seed-quantity-per-hectare-guide/">barley</a> or <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/eggplant-seed-quantity-per-hectare-planting-irrigation-tips/">Eggplant</a> They may require different patterns. Knowing the number of seeds or plants per hectare helps you calculate the space needed for irrigation.</li>\n<li><strong>Soil type:</strong> Sandy soils behave differently from clay soils regarding dripper flow rates and water infiltration rates. In clay soils, using higher-flow drippers or tape lines may be necessary to prevent surface saturation. Additionally, soil structure stability must be considered, as tape lines can be damaged in very loose soils.</li>\n<li><strong>Water source and quality:</strong> The presence of sediment, pollutants, and water hardness directly affects the service life of drippers and tape lines. If your water source has high levels of suspended solids, a more robust filtration system is required.</li>\n<li><strong>Tubing substrate:</strong> Selecting the appropriate bed for main lines, such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/90mm-plastic-pipe-irrigation-guide/">90 mm plastic pipe</a> or 90 mm textile pipe, is critical for reducing pressure loss and ensuring uniform water distribution along the entire row length. The wall thickness and material of these pipes must be selected according to the system operating pressure.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Performance comparison of drip tape systems</h2>\n<p>Drip tape is not a single product. Performance varies depending on thickness, material, and the number of internal rows. Understanding <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/types-irrigation-tapes-performance/">types of irrigation drip tape and their performance</a> for the specific crop is essential. Narrower tapes are more suitable for crops with fine roots and tight planting spacing, while wider tapes are used for greater coverage in crops with extensive root systems. Additionally, the UV resistance of the plastic material is vital in determining the useful life of the tape in outdoor conditions.</p>\n<p></p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-انتخاب-سیستم-آبیاری-برای-مزرعه-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع انتخاب سیستم آبیاری برای مزرعه - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Practical tips and technical recommendations for installation and maintenance</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Irrigation planning:</strong> Drip and tape systems are designed for precision irrigation. Avoid long-duration and high-flow irrigation cycles to prevent root stress and emitter failure. Calculating water requirements based on the regional evapotranspiration rate is key to success.</li>\n<li><strong>Water filtration:</strong> Installing an appropriate filter (disc or mesh) before water enters the system is mandatory to prevent clogging of drip and tape outlets. It is recommended to use filters with a 100 or 120 mesh screen.</li>\n<li><strong>Regular inspection:</strong> Periodically check drip and tape outlets for uniform flow and cloudy water. Uneven flow indicates clogging or wear. Flushing the system at appropriate times doubles equipment lifespan.</li>\n<li><strong>Fertigation:</strong> One of the biggest advantages of these systems is plant feeding (Fertigation). Use a dedicated tank to deliver nutrients directly to the roots with water. This method drastically increases the efficiency of pesticide and fertilizer use and reduces soil and air pollution.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>Is the strip tape system suitable for heavy soils?</h3>\n<p>Heavy (clay) soils have low infiltration rates. Using strip tape in these soil types can increase the risk of surface saturation and root asphyxiation. In such cases, a drip system with lower flow rates and shorter irrigation cycles is a safer option.</p>\n<h3>What is the difference between a dripper and a strip tape?</h3>\n<p>A dripper has point outlets that release water confined to a single point or a few points. Strip tape is a narrow plastic tube that distributes water over a broad, continuous strip on the soil surface. The choice between these two often depends on the planting row width and crop type.</p>\n<h3>Which system is better for tomato cultivation?</h3>\n<p>Tomatoes have deep and extensive root systems. A drip system is generally the standard option, unless planting is very dense and greater surface coverage is needed. In these conditions, strip tape may provide better performance due to its superior coverage. For more information, see the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/pomidor-support-tape-guide/">Pomodor support strip</a> guide.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-انتخاب-سیستم-آبیاری-برای-مزرعه-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع انتخاب سیستم آبیاری برای مزرعه - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h3>What are the most significant benefits of modern irrigation systems?</h3>\n<p>Precise irrigation application, a significant reduction in water and chemical inputs, labor savings, and automation capabilities. These benefits lead to improved farm economic efficiency.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h2>Conclusion and Final Recommendations</h2>\n<p>Selection <strong>of the Farm Irrigation System</strong> Choosing the appropriate farm irrigation system is a multi-factor decision-making process that must be based on precise data regarding soil, water, crops, and economic goals. Both drip and tape systems are powerful tools for modern farmers. The key to success lies in a deep understanding of your specific farm conditions and selecting a system that aligns with them. Through proper implementation and correct maintenance, you can benefit from optimized water use and elevate your crop production to a higher quality level. Always consult a specialized irrigation advisor before making a purchase to select the best option for your unique circumstances. For more details, review the specifications and features of tape irrigation.</p>','Comprehensive Guide to Selecting Farm Irrigation Systems: Drip and Tine Strip','This comprehensive guide compares drip and tape systems and explains the correct selection criteria based on crop type, soil, and water resources.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_navar_translation_queue_key','article-translation:strat-001:en-US' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key');
