SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: Why filter selection is critical in drip irrigation</h2>\n<p>Pressurized irrigation systems, particularly <strong>drip irrigation</strong> and strip emitters, offer high precision. Any suspended particles, sediment, algae, or even seeds in the source water can clog drip emitters or strip emitter tips. In fact, the filter is your only line of defense against these issues. Selecting the appropriate filter is not simply about purchasing a basic plastic component; it requires a deep understanding of water sources, crop types, and water chemistry.</p>\n<p>If you aim for high yields with sensitive crops, such as cereals and legumes, understanding filtration principles is essential. For example, in rain-fed cereal cultivation, precise moisture management via drip systems can significantly impact the seed rate of winter wheat per hectare and improve product quality. Therefore, investing in a properly selected filter directly affects the final production cost.</p>\n\n<>\n\n<h2>Determining filter type based on water source and clarity</h2>\n<p>The first step in <strong>selecting the appropriate filter for drip irrigation</strong>Water source evaluation. Water sources are broadly classified into surface (streams, qanats, springs) and underground (wells) categories. In clear groundwater, a disk filter is usually sufficient; however, for surface water where algae, moss, or layered particles may be present, a turbidity filter (screen + disk) must be used.</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Disk filters:</strong> Suitable for well water with low suspended solids. They offer high efficiency in removing fine particles and are easy to clean.</li>\n<li><strong>Turbidity filters (screen + disk):</strong> Suitable for surface water. The first stage, the screen, removes coarse particles, and the second stage, the disk, filters fine particles.</li>\n<li><strong>Cylindrical filters:</strong> Primarily used in drip line systems with very high flow rates.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>When your system involves celery drip lines or other germinated vegetables, the risk of clogging increases due to the small diameter of the drip line holes. Under these conditions, the filter precision (Mesh Size) must not exceed 120 to 150 mesh.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/انتخاب-فیلتر-مناسب-برای-آبیاری-قطرهای-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="انتخاب فیلتر مناسب برای آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Strategic Guide: Matching the Filter to the Drip Tape System</h2>\n<p>In row and block crops, drip tape is more efficient. For <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/corn-strip-tape-spacing-forage-corn/" target="_blank">selecting the drip tape spacing for forage corn</a> or other crops, the low pressure and low flow rate of drip tape systems cause fine particles to easily clog the flow path. Therefore, using a combination mesh and disc filter is recommended to provide both preventive and high particle rejection capacity.</p>\n\n<p>Additionally, water chemistry plays a key role in filter selection. If the water contains high levels of calcium carbonate or iron, using an acid pump (Sulfuric Acid) to adjust water pH and prevent precipitate in drippers is essential, in addition to the filter. This process, often discussed as water chemistry management in strategic irrigation guides, is practically ineffective without the appropriate filter.</p>\n\n<>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for filter installation and maintenance</h2>\n<p>Never forget the filter; especially after the system is shut down during cold seasons. <strong>Key points for optimal filter performance:</strong></p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Regular inspection:</strong> Check the input and output pressure of the filter using separate manometers. If the differential pressure exceeds 0.5 bar, it is time to clean the filter.</li>\n<li><strong>Proper cleaning:</strong> A disc filter should be opened and flushed while water is flowing, so that particles are removed by the fluid flow, not by hand.</li>\n<li><strong>Bypass mode:</strong> For filter flushing, always use the system\'s Bypass mode to reduce the pressure on the filter to zero.</li>\n<li><strong>Filter elements:</strong> In sieve or mesh filters, use higher-quality elements. Lower-grade elements, over prolonged use, release particles into the water and can damage emitters.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>One of the less significant factors is water temperature. During hot seasons, the rapid growth of algae in surface water increases. Under these conditions, disc filters must be inspected every 2 to 3 days. Additionally, the use of chlorine or hydrogen peroxide for water disinfection should be performed before the water enters the filter to eliminate algae and prevent clogging. Many farmers investing in pulses such as lentils and chickpeas can significantly increase blue lentil yield per hectare by following correct filtration principles.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/انتخاب-فیلتر-مناسب-برای-آبیاری-قطرهای-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="انتخاب فیلتر مناسب برای آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<>\n\n<h2>Proper filter structure and mesh precision</h2>\n<p>The mesh precision (mesh) must be compatible with the diameter of the dripper or tape nozzle. The general rule is that the size of suspended particles should be no larger than one-third of the outlet hole diameter of the system. For example, if your dripper has a 1.2 mm diameter, you should use a filter with 120 mesh precision (approximately 0.4 mm).</p>\n\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Irrigation system type</th>\n<th>Recommended mesh precision</th>\n<th>Safe filter type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Conventional dripper (4-5 liter)</td>\n<td>80 - 120 mesh</td>\n<td>Screen or Mesh</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Self-regulating dripper (with flow regulator)</td>\n<td>120 - 150 mesh</td>\n<td>Disk (preferably with backwash)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tape</td>\n<td>150 - 170 mesh</td>\n<td>Disk + Mesh (Turbulex)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>It should be noted that installing a mesh filter before the disk filter extends the useful life of the disk filter and reduces the need for cleaning. In this setup, a mesh filter with a precision of 200 filters fine particles, allowing only coarse particles to reach the disk filter. For those working in large-scale systems, refer to the comprehensive guide. <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/lif-flat-pipe-price-guide-tajikistan/" target="_blank">Price of Life Filters in Tajikistan and Local Markets</a> It can provide them with a better economic perspective on system maintenance costs.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n\n<h3>How do I know if my filter is clogged?</h3>\n<p>The best way to measure the pressure drop before and after the filter is with a dual-port pressure gauge. If the pressure drop exceeds 0.5 km of head, the filter is clogging and requires cleaning.</p>\n\n<h3>Are cartridge filters suitable for surface water?</h3>\n<p>Cartridge filters can be used for surface water; however, due to their limited internal space and difficulty in cleaning, combined mesh and ring-disc filters are generally the first choice for turbid water containing algae. Unless your system strictly requires more precise filtration, in which case polymer cartridges with replaceable cores are a better option.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/انتخاب-فیلتر-مناسب-برای-آبیاری-قطرهای-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="انتخاب فیلتر مناسب برای آبیاری قطره‌ای - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h3>At what pressure should the filter be opened?</h3>\n<p>Never open the filter when the system is running without activating the Bypass mode. Water pressure can quickly and dangerously rebound. Always close the main valves first to bring the pressure on the filter to zero.</p>\n\n<h2>Final Summary</h2>\n<p>Selecting the appropriate filter for drip irrigation is not a simple purchase decision; it is an engineering process requiring an understanding of water quality, system type, and cropping objectives. From disk filters for clear well water to turbo composite filters for surface water, each has a specific application. Remember that proper maintenance and timely cleaning can double or triple the service life of drippers and tape lines, while significantly reducing repair and replacement costs. In grain and vegetable crops, attention to these details directly impacts yields of apples per hectare and other fruit and grain products. By investing in a systematic filtration setup, you can ensure the health and sustainability of your irrigation system.</p>\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%da%af%d9%86%d8%af%d9%85-%d8%af%db%8c%d9%85-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Rainfed Wheat Seed Rate per Hectare: A Comprehensive Cultivation Guide</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%aa%d9%86%d8%a7%da%98-%d8%b9%d8%af%d8%b3-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Lentil Tonnage per Hectare: Influencing Factors + Methods to Increase</a></p>','Comprehensive Guide to Selecting the Right Filter for Drip and Tape Irrigation','The filter is the beating heart of drip and tape irrigation systems. This article provides a complete guide to selecting the best filter type based on irrigation method, suspended particle size, and budget, ensuring your system\'s efficiency is maximized.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
