SET @resolved_conflict=(SELECT ID FROM `ha_posts` WHERE post_name=@resolved_slug AND post_type='post' AND (@translation_id IS NULL OR ID<>@translation_id) LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: Why is Calculating ET0 Important for Farmers?</h2>\n<p>Optimal irrigation cannot be achieved without a proper understanding of plant physiology and climatic conditions. In drip and micro-sprinkler irrigation systems, accuracy in calculating water requirements directly impacts production costs, soil health, and final yield. The key parameter in this process is the reference evapotranspiration (ET0) value. ET0 indicates how much water a reference plant surface loses through evaporation and transpiration. To <strong>Calculate Water Requirements Based on ET0</strong>, this reference value must be multiplied by the crop coefficient (Kc) of the specific crop to obtain the crop evapotranspiration (ETc). This method eliminates guesswork and transforms irrigation into a precise science. Correctly understanding this process is the key to preventing root drought or over-irrigation, both of which lead to reduced economic efficiency of the farm. Additionally, proper sowing and farmer knowledge during the planting stage have a direct impact on irrigation potential. To learn about one of the important products, you can refer to the article <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%af%d8%a7%d9%85-%d8%b2%d9%85%db%8c%d9%86%db%8c-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Peanut Seed Rate per Hectare + Influencing Factors</a> to better understand how planting density affects water requirements.</p>\n<h2>Basic Concepts: ET0, Kc, and ETc</h2>\n<p>For a deeper understanding, the three main concepts must be examined individually. First, ET0, which is a daily variable value measured in millimeters. Second, Kc, known as the crop coefficient, which indicates the difference in water requirements between the crop and the reference surface. Third, ETc, which is the product of these two values. Always remember the simple relationship below: <strong>ETc = ET0 × Kc</strong>. The plant coefficient (Kc) varies depending on the plant type, growth stage, and environmental conditions. For example, Kc is low during the seedling stage and peaks during the fruiting stage. In crops such as beans, managing row spacing is critical; you can read the article on standard optimal spacing for row planting in beans to better understand how layout affects moisture distribution. Additionally, understanding the appropriate seed rate for each crop is important; the guide on garlic seed rate per hectare: influencing factors and solutions can serve as an example of factors affecting water requirements.</p>\n\n<h2>ET0 Calculation Methods: From Fetch to Forough</h2>\n<p>The most accurate method for calculating ET0 is using the FAO Penman-Monteith equation, recommended by the Food and Agriculture Organization. This equation considers variables such as temperature, relative humidity, wind speed, and solar radiation. For farmers who do not have access to a weather station, simpler methods such as Rat or Masten-Simms are available, which use temperature and radiation data. & Simms) exist. If precise data are required, using small weather stations or local tele-meteorological sensing increases calculation accuracy. In ginger crops, which are highly sensitive to moisture, the precision of these calculations is essential. You can consider the guide on mung bean yield per hectare: a comprehensive guide for increasing yield and efficiency as another example of the link between proper irrigation and final yield. Additionally, for orchard crops, understanding the carrot seed rate per hectare helps better understand water demand during early growth stages.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/محاسبه-نیاز-آبی-گیاه-بر-اساس-et0-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="محاسبه نیاز آبی گیاه بر اساس ET0 - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h2>Impact of Irrigation System Type on ETC Consumption</h2>\n<p>Tape and drip irrigation systems deliver water only to the root zone, whereas sprinkler systems irrigate the entire surface. In tape systems, a significant portion of ET0 is reduced by soil surface evaporation because part of the surface is sloped. Therefore, when <strong>calculating water requirements based on ET0</strong> In drip systems, we typically apply a quantity less than the calculated ETc. This reduction is due to partial root coverage and decreased surface evaporation. Conversely, in arid regions, increased tape irrigation can lead to relative soil dryness. Therefore, adjusting tape spacing and drip emitter discharge rates should be calibrated according to the local ET0. Proper tape installation training is also important; the guide <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/type-irrigation-tape-installation-method/">type irrigation tape installation method</a> can help prevent water loss during the initial stage. Finally, for optimizing performance in market crops, studying <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/piyozcha-hosili-gektar-rohnomo/">piyozcha hosili gektar rohnomo</a> is also useful regarding the relationship between irrigation dosage and yield. Additionally, trees requiring precise irrigation, such as walnuts, require more accurate calculations; you can search for <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/lentil-yield-per-hectare-iraq/">lentil yield per hectare iraq</a> patterns from other crops as well.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for optimization using ET0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Weekly ET0 monitoring:</strong> Use data from the local weather station to update ET0 values. These values change significantly with the seasons.</li>\n<li><strong>Adjusting Kc based on growth stage:</strong> Follow Kc tables for different crops. During the emergence stage, Kc is approximately 0.4, while it reaches 1.2 or higher during peak growth.</li>\n<li><strong>Soil porosity and low-flow irrigation:</strong> In drip systems, using lower flow rates with more frequent irrigation cycles maintains moisture in the root zone and prevents nutrient leaching.</li>\n<li><strong>Balance between irrigation and ventilation:</strong> When relative humidity is high, plant transpiration slows down. Consider this factor in your calculations to prevent over-irrigation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Additionally, maintaining drip systems is essential to preserve accuracy in crop water requirement calculations. Clogged emitters lead to uneven water distribution and, consequently, variations in ETc among different plants. Guide <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/drip-tape-maintenance-costs/">drip tape maintenance costs</a> It can provide an estimate of your operational costs. It can also help farmers using newer drip systems gain better insights through study. <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/irrigation-tape-squash-guide/">irrigation tape squash guide</a> It can provide a better understanding of technical challenges. Selecting the appropriate drip emitter spacing based on local ET0 is also important; in this regard, the guide <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/gafsii-devori-lentai-obyorii-qatragi/">gafsii devori lentai obyorii qatragi</a> provides you with useful information.</p>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>Is ET0 constant or does it change?</h3>\n<p>ET0 is highly variable and changes based on season, climate, temperature, relative humidity, wind speed, and daily solar radiation. In midsummer, ET0 can be twice as high as in winter. These fluctuations directly affect your daily irrigation requirements and need precise adjustment.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/محاسبه-نیاز-آبی-گیاه-بر-اساس-et0-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="محاسبه نیاز آبی گیاه بر اساس ET0 - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h3>How do I find my plant\'s Kc?</h3>\n<p>Use FAO reference tables or local irrigation guides. These coefficients vary by growth stage (seedling, vegetative, flowering, fruiting). If local data are unavailable, you can use global averages for similar crops and then calibrate by monitoring plant growth.</p>\n<h3>Do I need the full ET0 in a strip irrigation system?</h3>\n<p>No, usually you only replace a portion of ETc (for example, 70 to 80 percent) because part of the soil surface remains dry. Accurate calculation based on ET0 allows you to manage this reduction factor and prevent over-irrigation.</p>\n\n\n<h2>Conclusion: Data-Driven Smart Irrigation</h2>\n<p>Use of <strong>Calculating irrigation requirements based on ET0</strong> is not just a mathematical formula, but a smart approach to managing water resources. By combining weather data, understanding the crop coefficient, and selecting the appropriate irrigation system (drip or strip), you can reduce water consumption by up to 30 percent while simultaneously increasing yield. This method provides a scientific basis for transforming conventional agriculture into precision agriculture. To deepen your knowledge, you can review related topics such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%af%d8%a7%d9%85-%d8%b2%d9%85%db%8c%d9%86%db%8c-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Peanut seed rate per hectare + influencing factors</a> to understand the relationship between planting and irrigation. Also, considering the total water volume in the soil profile (related subheadings) can provide a more comprehensive view of your farm\'s water budget.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/محاسبه-نیاز-آبی-گیاه-بر-اساس-et0-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="محاسبه نیاز آبی گیاه بر اساس ET0 - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> Peanut Seed Rate per Hectare + Influencing Factors</p>\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> Peanut Seed Rate per Hectare + Influencing Factors</p>','Guide to Calculating Crop Water Needs Using ET0: Drip and Tape Irrigation','In this article, we examine the principles of calculating ET0 and its impact on irrigation doses in drip and tape system. By understanding the relationship between the crop coefficient (Kc) and ET0, reduce water consumption and increase crop yield.','publish','closed','closed',@resolved_slug,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL;
SET @translation_id=COALESCE(@translation_id,IF(@source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @resolved_conflict IS NULL,LAST_INSERT_ID(),NULL));
